# Traffic Steering xApp patch set, applied in this order with git apply to the commit pinned in commit_hashes.json
# (additional_scripts/install_xapp_traffic_steering.sh). Paths are relative to install_patch_files/xApps/ts/; each
# patch names the file it changes in its diff header. The installer first restores every file the patches change,
# then applies them in order. The trafficxapp image's patchset.sha256 label derives from this file and the files
# it lists.
# A1 policy body sent as a JSON string by the Go a1mediator (3.x)
src/ts_xapp/ts_xapp.cpp.patch
# do-nothing default RMR handler (a stray 12041/12042 is otherwise freed twice by xapp-frame-cpp 2.3.6)
src/ts_xapp/ts_xapp.cpp.default_handler.patch
# cell keys only from NR nodes (en_gnb_/gnb_ meids), read from the hex text of the X2 request part that e2mgr keeps
src/ts_xapp/ts_xapp.cpp.nr_cell_map.patch
# gRPC UeId field 2 enGNBUEID (the RC UE ID en-gNB-UEID): rc.proto as rc patch 0003 has it, and rc.pb.cc/rc.pb.h
# generated from it by protoc 3.6.1 (the toolchain of the committed files; rc.grpc.pb.* are unchanged)
ext/protobuf/rc.proto.patch
ext/protobuf/rc.pb.cc.patch
ext/protobuf/rc.pb.h.patch
# DC PSCell Change control (E2SM-RC CONTROL Style 5 action 3) to the source en-gNB, the node of the serving cell
# the QP prediction names first; the RC UE ID en-gNB-UEID is parsed from the ueId tag kpimon writes, and the control
# is sent only when a UeMetrics point carries exactly that tag (Influx v2 query; descriptor controls influx_*,
# set by the installer); the tag parser, the reader of the query's annotated CSV answer (an HTTP 200 answer can be an
# error table) and their unit test, which make runs
src/ts_xapp/en_gnb_ue_id.hpp.patch
src/ts_xapp/influx_csv.hpp.patch
src/ts_xapp/en_gnb_ue_id_test.cpp.patch
src/ts_xapp/CMakeLists.txt.patch
src/ts_xapp/ts_xapp.cpp.style5_en_gnb_ueid.patch
